The attached image displays confocal microscopy of bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) demonstrating the uptake of Nano-11 nanoparticles and ovalbumin (OVA). When BMDCs were incubated with soluble OVA alone, minimal uptake was observed (green fluorescence). In contrast, incubation with Nano-11 (red fluorescence) or OVA adsorbed to Nano-11 resulted in efficient internalization by BMDCs. The merged images clearly show significant colocalization of OVA and Nano-11 (yellow), indicating that OVA remains associated with Nano-11 within the cells. This illustrates Nano-11's ability to enhance antigen delivery to dendritic cells, a critical step for vaccine adjuvant function.